to be”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> ācariya</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> ādiyati (“to take”)</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> ādiyati, which is masculine/neuter locative singular of <i>ආදියන‍්ත්</i> &#x20;(ādiyant), present participle of the verb</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> ādiyant, which is present active participle of <i>ආදියති</i> &#x20;(ādiyati, “to take”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> āpajjati (“to undergo”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> āmanteti</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> āmantesi, being second/third-person singular aorist active of <i>ආමන‍්තෙති</i> &#x20;(āmanteti)</li><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> āmantesi, being second-person singular present active of <i>ආමන‍්තෙති</i> &#x20;(āmanteti)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> āruyha, absolutive of <i>ආරුහති</i> &#x20;(āruhati, “to ascend”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> āruhati (“to ascend”)</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> āruhati, masculine/neuter locative singular of <i>ආරුහන‍්ත්</i> &#x20;(āruhant), <i>present active participle of the verb above</i></li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> āvasatha (“place of abode”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> āsana</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> āhattar (“bringer”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> āhattā, <i>which is</i> nominative/vocative singular/plural of <i>ආහත‍්තර්</i> &#x20;(āhattar, “bringer”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> āhattu, <i>which is</i> genitive/dative singular of <i>ආහත‍්තර්</i> &#x20;(āhattar, “bringer”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> indriya (“faculty”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> ima (“this”)</li></ol><p><b>Pronoun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> ima (“this”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Particle</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> iva (“like, as”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> issa</li></ol><p>Compare Sanskrit <i>ऋक्ष</i> (ṛkṣa)</p></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> isso, nominative singular of <i>ඉස‍්ස</i> &#x20;(issa, “bear”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> uju</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> uttarati (“to cross over”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> uttarasetu (“bridge”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> uttareyyaṃ, first-person singular optative active of <i>උත‍්තරති</i> &#x20;(uttarati, “to cross over”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Contraction</b></p><ol><li><i>As</i> first-person singular optative active of <i>උත‍්තරති</i> &#x20;(uttarati) <i>at the end of a quotation</i>.</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> udakaṇṇava (“flood of water”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> udakaṇṇavo, <i>which is</i> nominative singular of <i>උදකණ‍්ණව</i> &#x20;(udakaṇṇava, “flood of water”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> upagañchi, being third-person singular aorist active of <i>උපගච‍්ඡති</i> &#x20;(upagacchati)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> upagacchati (“to approach”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> upanayhati (“to bind up”)</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> upanayhati, masculine/neuter locative singular of <i>උපනය‍්හන‍්ත්</i> &#x20;(upanayhant), <i>present active participle of the verb above</i></li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> upasaṅkamati</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> upasaṅkamati, <i>which is</i> masculine/neuter locative singular of <i>උපසඞ‍්කමන‍්ත්</i> &#x20;(upasaṅkamant), <i>present active participle of the verb above</i></li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> upasaṅkami, second/third-person singular aorist active of <i>උපසඞ‍්කමති</i> &#x20;(upasaṅkamati)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> upasaṅkamitvā, being absolutive of <i>උපසඞ‍්කමති</i> &#x20;(upasaṅkamati)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> upasammati (“to subside”)</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> upasammati, <i>which is</i> masculine/neuter locative singular of <i>උපසම‍්මන‍්ත්</i> &#x20;(upasammant), <i>present active participle of the verb above</i></li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Pronoun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> ubha (“both”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Numeral</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> ubho, nominative/accusative masculine/feminine/neuter of <i>උභ</i> &#x20;(ubha, “both”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Numeral</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> eka (“one”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> ekāgārika (“robber”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> eko, <i>which is</i> nominative singular masculine of <i>එක</i> &#x20;(eka, “one”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> eta</li></ol><p><b>Pronoun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> eta</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Tai Tham script form of</i> etad, <i>which is</i> nominative/accusative singular neuter of <i>එත</i> &#x20;(eta, “this”)</li></ol><p><b>Pronoun</b></p><ol><li><i>Tai Tham script form of</i> etad, <i>which is</i> nominative/accusative singular of <i>එත</i> &#x20;(eta, “this one”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Particle</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> etarahi</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adverb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> ettha ("here")</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Particle</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> eva (“even”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Particle</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> evaṃ</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> orima (“on this side”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> orimo, alternative citation form of <i>ඔරිම</i>&#x20;(<i>orima</i>, “on this side”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> oluggavilugga (“falling to pieces”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> oluggaviluggo, nominative singular masculine of <i>ඔලුග‍්ගවිලුග‍්ග</i> &#x20;(oluggavilugga, “falling to pieces”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Pronoun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> ka (“who (m.)”)</li><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> ka (“what”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> kaṭṭha (“a stick”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> kaṭṭhaṃ, nominative/accusative singular of <i>කට‍්ඨ</i> &#x20;(kaṭṭha, “a stick”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Particle</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> kathaṃ (“how?”)</li></ol><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> kathaṃ, <i>which is</i> accusative singular of <i>කථා</i> &#x20;(kathā, “story”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> kathā</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> karīyati, which is passive of <i>කරොති</i> &#x20;(karoti, “to do”)</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> karīyati, which is masculine/neuter locative singular of <i>කරීයන‍්ත්</i> &#x20;(karīyant), present participle of the verb above</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> karoti (“to do”)</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> karoti, which is masculine/neuter locative singular of <i>කරොන‍්ත්</i> &#x20;(karont), present participle of the verb above</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> karont, which is present participle of <i>කරොති</i> &#x20;(karoti, “to do”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Pronoun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> kā (“who (f.)”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li>alternative form of <i>කාරෙති</i>&#x20;(<i>kāreti</i>) and <i>Sinhala script form of</i> kārayati, which is a causative of <i>කරොති</i> &#x20;(karoti, “to do”)</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> kārayati, which is masculine/neuter locative singular of <i>කාරයන‍්ත්</i> &#x20;(kārayant), present participle of the verb</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> kārayant, which is present participle of <i>කාරයති</i> &#x20;(kārayati)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li>causative of <i>කරොති</i> &#x20;(karoti, “to do”)</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> kāreti, which is masculine/neuter locative singular of <i>කාරෙන‍්ත්</i> &#x20;(kārent), present participle of the verb</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> kilamati (“to be weary”)</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> kilamati, masculine/neuter locative singular of <i>කිලමන‍්ත‍්</i> &#x20;(kilamant), which is present participle of the verb above</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li>alternative form of <i>කිලමෙති</i>&#x20;(<i>kilameti</i>) and <i>Sinhala script form of</i> kilamayati, causative of <i>කිලමති</i> &#x20;(kilamati, “to do”)</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li>masculine/neuter locative singular of <i>කිලමයන‍්ත්</i> &#x20;(kilamayant), present participle of the verb above</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> kilamayant, present participle of <i>කිලමෙති</i> &#x20;(kilameti), causative of <i>කිලමති</i> &#x20;(kilamati, “to be weary”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li>alternative form of <i>කිලමාපෙති</i>&#x20;(<i>kilamāpeti</i>) and <i>Sinhala script form of</i> kilamāpayati, double causative of <i>කිලමති</i> &#x20;(kilamati, “to be weary”)</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> kilamāpayati, which is masculine/neuter locative singular of <i>කිලමාපයන‍්ත්</i> &#x20;(kilamāpayant), present participle of the verb above</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> kilamāpayato, masculine/neuter genitive/dative singular of <i>කිලමාපයන‍්ත්</i> &#x20;(kilamāpayant), which is a present participle of <i>කිලමාපෙති</i> &#x20;(kilamāpeti), double causative of <i>කිලමති</i> &#x20;(kilamati, “to do”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> kilamāpayant, present participle of <i>කිලමාපෙති</i> &#x20;(kilamāpeti), double causative of <i>කිලමති</i> &#x20;(kilamati, “to be weary”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> kilamāpeti, double causative of <i>කිලමති</i> &#x20;(kilamati, “to be weary”)</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> kilamāpeti, which is masculine/neuter locative singular of <i>කිලමාපෙන‍්ත්</i> &#x20;(kilamāpent), present participle of the verb above</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> kilameti, which is causative of <i>කිලමති</i> &#x20;(kilamati)</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li>masculine/neuter locative singular of <i>කිලමෙන‍්ත්</i> &#x20;(kilament), present participle of the verb above</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adverb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> kudācanaṃ (“at any time”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> kulla (“raft”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> kullo, nominative singular of <i>කුල‍්ල</i> &#x20;(kulla, “raft”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> khema (“safe”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> khemo, nominative singular masculine of <i>ඛෙම</i> &#x20;(khema, “safe”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Particle</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> kho</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> gacchati</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> gacchati, which is masculine/neuter locative singular of <i>ගච‍්ඡන‍්ත්</i> &#x20;(gacchant), present participle of the verb above</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> gacchant, which is present active participle of <i>ගච‍්ඡති</i> &#x20;(gacchati, “to go”)</li></ol></html><