<li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> chedāpayati, <i>which is</i> masculine/neuter locative singular of <i>ඡෙදාපයන‍්ත්</i> &#x20;(chedāpayant), <i>present participle of the verb</i></li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> jayati, <i>which is an</i> alternative form of <i>ජෙති</i>&#x20;(<i>jeti</i>, “to win”), which see for further information.</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> jayati, <i>which is</i> masculine and neuter locative singular of <i>ජයන‍්ත්</i> &#x20;(jayant), <i>present participle of the verb above</i></li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> jara (“old”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> jaro, nominative singular masculine of <i>ජර</i> &#x20;(jara, “old”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> jīvita (“life”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> jeti (“to win”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> jhāna</li></ol><p>Inherited from Sanskrit <i>ध्यान</i> (dhyāna).</p></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li>(<i>demonstrative</i>) <i>Sinhala script form of</i> ta ("that")</li></ol><p><b>Pronoun</b></p><ol><li>(<i>demonstrative</i>) <i>Sinhala script form of</i> ta ("he, it")</li><li>(<i>demonstrative</i>) <i>Sinhala script form of</i> ta ("it")</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adverb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> taṃ (“there”)</li><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> taṃ (“therefore”)</li></ol><p><b>Pronoun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> taṃ, which is accusative singular of <i>ත</i> &#x20;(ta, “he, it”)</li><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> taṃ, which is nominative/accusative singular of <i>ත</i> &#x20;(ta, “it”)</li><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> taṃ, which is accusative singular of <i>තා</i> &#x20;(tā, “she, it”)</li><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> taṃ, which is accusative singular of <i>ත්‍වං</i> &#x20;(tvaṃ, “you”)</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> taṃ, which is accusative singular masculine/feminine of <i>ත</i> &#x20;(ta, “that”)</li><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> taṃ, which is nominative/accusative singular neuter of <i>ත</i> &#x20;(ta, “that”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adverb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> tatra</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adverb</b></p><ol><li><i>Devanagari script form of</i> tathā (“in that way”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Pronoun</b></p><ol><li>(<i>demonstrative</i>) <i>Sinhala script form of</i> tassa, <i>which is</i> genitive/dative singular of <i>ත</i> &#x20;(ta, “he, it”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Pronoun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> tvaṃ ("you")</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> tiṭṭhati (“to stand”)</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> tiṭṭhati, <i>which is</i> masculine/neuter locative singular of <i>තිට‍්ඨන‍්ත්</i> &#x20;(tiṭṭhant), <i>present participle of the verb above</i></li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> tiṭṭhant, which is present active participle of <i>තිට‍්ඨති</i> &#x20;(tiṭṭhati, “to stand”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> tiṇa (“grass”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> tiṇaṃ, nominative/accusative singular of <i>තිණ</i> &#x20;(tiṇa, “grass”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> tīra (“shore”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> tīraṃ, <i>which is</i> nominative/accusative singular of <i>තීර</i> &#x20;(tīra, “shore”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> tuṭṭha, <i>which is</i> past participle of <i>තුස‍්සති</i> &#x20;(tussati, “to be satisfied”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> tuṭṭho, <i>which is</i> nominative singular masculine of <i>තුට‍්ඨ</i> &#x20;(tuṭṭha), <i>which is</i> past participle of <i>තුස‍්සති</i> &#x20;(tussati, “to be satisfied”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adverb</b></p><ol><li>there</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> tena, masculine/neuter instrumental singular of <i>ta</i> (“that (<i>demonstrative</i>)”)</li></ol><p><b>Pronoun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> tena, instrumental singular of <i>ta</i> (“him, it, that”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> thapati (“builder; officer”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> dadāti (“to give”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> dvāra</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> dinna, which is past participle of <i>දදාති</i> &#x20;(dadāti, “to give”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> disvā, <i>which is</i> absolutive of <i>පස‍්සති</i> &#x20;(passati, “to see”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li>to point out</li><li>to teach</li><li>to preach</li><li>to expound</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li>masculine and neuter locative singular of <i>දෙසෙන‍්ත්</i> &#x20;(desent), present participle of the verb above</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> domanassa (“dejectedness”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> dvāra (“door”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> dvāraṃ, <i>which is</i> nominative/accusative singular of <i>ද‍්වාර</i> &#x20;(dvāra, “door”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> dhamma (“righteousness”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> dhīra (“wise; firm”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> dhīro, nominative singular masculine of <i>ධීර</i> &#x20;(dhīra, “wise; firm”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Particle</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> na</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> na (“that”)</li></ol><p><b>Pronoun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> na (“him, it, that”)</li><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> na (“it, that”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Contraction</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> natthi (“there is not”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> nāga (“serpent”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> nāgo, <i>which is</i> nominative singular of <i>නාග</i> &#x20;(nāga, “serpent”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> nāma (“name”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> nāvā (“boat”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> nipaccākāra (“respect”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> nillopa (“plunder”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> nisajja, <i>which is</i> absolutive of <i>නිසීදති</i> &#x20;(nisīdati, “to sit down”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> nisīdati (“to sit down”)</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> nisīdati, <i>which is</i> masculine/neuter locative singular of <i>නිසීදන‍්ත්</i> &#x20;(nisīdant), <i>present participle of the verb above</i></li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> nisīdi, being second/third-person singular aorist active of <i>නිසීදති</i> &#x20;(nisīdati)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> nissayati (“to rest on”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> nissāya, absolutive of <i>නිස‍්සයති</i> &#x20;(nissayati, “to rest on”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Particle</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> nu (“then, now”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> nudati (“to push”)</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> nudati, masculine/neuter locative singular of <i>නුදන‍්ත්</i> &#x20;(nudant), <i>present active participle of the verb above</i></li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Pronoun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> no, <i>which is</i> accusative/instrumental/genitive/dative plural of <i>අහං</i> &#x20;(ahaṃ, “us”)</li></ol><p><b>Particle</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> no (“surely not”)</li><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> no (“indeed”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pacati (“to cook”)</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li>masculine/neuter locative singular of <i>පචන‍්ත්</i> &#x20;(pacant), present participle of the verb above</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> paccorohati (“to descend”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> paccorohitvā, absolutive of <i>පච‍්චොරොහති</i> &#x20;(paccorohati, “to descend”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> paññatta, being past participle of <i>පඤ‍්ඤාපෙති</i> &#x20;(paññāpeti)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> paññā (“wisdom”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> paññāpeti</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> paṭipajjati (“to follow a route”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> paṭipanna (“following a route”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> paṭipanno, <i>which is</i> nominative singular masculine of <i>පටිපන‍්න</i> &#x20;(paṭipanna, “following a route”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> paṇḍita (“wise man”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> paṇṇa</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> paṇṇaṃ, nominative/accusative singular of <i>පණ‍්ණ</i> &#x20;(paṇṇa, “leaf”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> patati (“to fall”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pattika (“on foot”)</li></ol><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pattika (“pedestrian”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pattiko, nominative singular masculine of <i>පත‍්තික</i> &#x20;(pattika, “on foot”)</li></ol><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pattiko, nominative singular of <i>පත‍්තික</i> &#x20;(pattika, “pedestrian”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> padātar (“bestower”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> padātā, <i>which is</i> nominative/vocative singular/plural of <i>පදාතර්</i> &#x20;(padātar, “bestower”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> padātu, <i>which is</i> genitive/dative singular of <i>පදාතර්</i> &#x20;(padātar, “bestower”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Particle</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pana</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pantha</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pabbata (“mountain”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pabbato, nominative singular of <i>පබ‍්බත</i> &#x20;(pabbata, “mountain”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pamāda (“heedlessness”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pamādo, nominative singular of <i>පමාද</i> &#x20;(pamāda, “heedlessness”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> payirupāsaṃ, nominative/vocative singular masculine/neuter & accusative singular neuter of <i>පයිරුපාසන‍්ත්</i> &#x20;(payirupāsant), <i>which is</i> present active participle of <i>පයිරුපාසති</i> &#x20;(payirupāsati, “to attend on”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> payirupāsati (“to attend on”)</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> payirupāsati, masculine/neuter locative singular of <i>පයිරුපාසන‍්ත්</i> &#x20;(payirupāsant), <i>present active participle of the verb above</i></li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> payirupāsant, present active participle of <i>පයිරුපාසති</i> &#x20;(payirupāsati, “to attend on”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> para (“other”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> paradāra (“someone else's wife”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> paradāraṃ, which is accusative singular of <i>පරදාර</i> &#x20;(paradāra, “someone else's wife”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> paradāraṃ gacchati (“to commit adultery”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> paripantha (“edge of the road”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> paripanthe, <i>which is</i> inflection of <i>පරිපන්‍ථ</i>:## locative singular## accusative plural &#x20;(paripantha, “edge of the road”)</li></ol><p><b>Adverb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> paripanthe (“in ambush”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> paribbājaka</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pariyāya</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pariyāyo, <i>which is</i> nominative singular of <i>පරියාය</i> &#x20;(pariyāya, “course”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> paro, <i>which is</i> nominative singular masculine of <i>පර</i> &#x20;(para, “other”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> palāsa (“leaf”)</li><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> palāsa (“foliage”)</li><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> palāsa (“bastard teak”)</li><li>alternative form of <i>පළාස</i>&#x20;(<i>paḷāsa</i>, “mercilessness”)</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> palāsa (“green”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> palāsaṃ, nominative/accusative singular of <i>පලාස</i> &#x20;(palāsa, “leaf”)</li><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> palāsaṃ, nominative/accusative singular of <i>පලාස</i> &#x20;(palāsa, “foliage”)</li><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> palāsaṃ, accusative singular of <i>පලාස</i> &#x20;(palāsa, “bastard teak”)</li><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> palāsaṃ, accusative singular of <i>පලාස</i> &#x20;(palāsa, “mercilessness”)</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> palāsaṃ, nominative singular neuter and accusative singular masculine/neuter of <i>පලාස</i> &#x20;(palāsa, “green”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> palāso, nominative singular of <i>පලාස</i> &#x20;(palāsa, “leaf”)</li><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> palāso, nominative singular of <i>පලාස</i> &#x20;(palāsa, “bastard teak”)</li><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> palāso, nominative singular of <i>පලාස</i> &#x20;(palāsa, “mercilessness”)</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> palāso, nominative singular masculine of <i>පලාස</i> &#x20;(palāsa, “green”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> passaṃ, nominative/vocative singular masculine/neuter & accusative singular neuter of <i>පස‍්සන‍්ත්</i> &#x20;(passant), <i>which is</i> present active participle of <i>පස‍්සති</i> &#x20;(passati, “to see”)</li></ol><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> passaṃ, accusative singular of <i>පස‍්ස</i> &#x20;(passa, “one who sees”)</li><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> passaṃ, nominative/accusative singular of <i>පස‍්ස</i> &#x20;(passa, “flank”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> passati (“to see”)</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> passati, <i>which is</i> masculine/neuter locative singular of <i>පස‍්සන‍්ත්</i> &#x20;(passant), <i>present participle of the verb above</i></li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> passant, present active participle of <i>පස‍්සති</i> &#x20;(passati, “to see”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li>alternative form of <i>පාචෙති</i>&#x20;(<i>pāceti</i>) <i>and</i> <i>Sinhala script form of</i> pācayati, causative of <i>පචති</i> &#x20;(pacati, “to cook”)</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pācayati, <i>which is</i> masculine/neuter locative singular of <i>පාචයන‍්ත්</i> &#x20;(pācayant), <i>present participle of the verb above</i></li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pācayant, present participle of <i>පාචෙති</i> &#x20;(pāceti), causative of <i>පචති</i> &#x20;(pacati, “to cook”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pāceti, <i>which is</i> causative of <i>පචති</i> &#x20;(pacati)</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li>masculine/neuter locative singular of <i>පාචන‍්ත්</i> &#x20;(pācant), <i>present participle of the verb above</i></li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pāṇabhūta (“living being”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pāṇabhūto, <i>which is</i> nominative singular of <i>පාණභූත</i> &#x20;(pāṇabhūta, “living being”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li>alternative form of <i>පාණමතිපාතෙති</i>&#x20;(<i>pāṇamatipāteti</i>) <i>and</i> <i>Sinhala script form of</i> pāṇamatipātayati (“to kill a living being”)</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pāṇamatipātayati, <i>which is</i> masculine/neuter locative singular of <i>පාණමතිපාතයන‍්ත්</i> &#x20;(pāṇamatipātayant), <i>present participle of the verb</i></li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pāṇamatipātayato, which is masculine/neuter genitive/dative singular of <i>පාණමතිපාතයන‍්ත්</i> &#x20;(pāṇamatipātayant, “to kill a living being”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pāṇamatipātayant, <i>which is</i> present active participle of <i>පාණමතිපාතෙති</i> &#x20;(pāṇamatipāteti, “to kill a living being”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pāṇamatipāteti</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pāṇamatipāteti, <i>which is</i> masculine/neuter locative singular of <i>පාණමතිපාතෙන‍්ත්</i> &#x20;(pāṇamatipātent), <i>present participle of the verb</i></li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pātayati, causative of <i>පතති</i> &#x20;(patati, “to fall”) and alternative form of <i>පාතෙති</i>&#x20;(<i>pāteti</i>)</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pātayati, <i>which is</i> masculine/neuter locative singular of <i>පාතයන‍්ත්</i> &#x20;(pātayant), present participle of the verb</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pātayant, present participle of <i>පාතෙති</i> &#x20;(pāteti), causative of <i>පතති</i> &#x20;(patati, “to fall”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pāteti, <i>which see, which is</i> causative of <i>පතති</i> &#x20;(patati)</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pāteti, <i>which is</i> masculine/neuter locative singular of <i>පාතෙන‍්ත්</i> &#x20;(pātent), <i>present participle of the verb</i></li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pāda (“foot”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pādaṃ, nominative/accusative singular of <i>පාද</i> &#x20;(pāda, “foot”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pādo, nominative singular of <i>පාද</i> &#x20;(pāda, “foot”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pāpa (“evil”)</li></ol><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pāpa (“sin”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pāpaṃ, nominative singular masculine and accusative singular masculine/neuter of <i>පාප</i> &#x20;(pāpa, “evil”)</li></ol><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pāpaṃ, nominative/accusative singular of <i>පාප</i> &#x20;(pāpa, “sin”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li>evil</li><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pāpaka (“evil”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pāpo, nominative singular masculine of <i>පාප</i> &#x20;(pāpa, “evil”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adverb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pāra (“beyond”)</li></ol><p><b>Preposition</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pāra (“beyond”)</li></ol><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pāra (“the other side”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pāraṃ, nominative/accusative singular of <i>පාර</i> &#x20;(pāra, “the other side”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pārima (“farther”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pārimo, alternative citation form of <i>පාරිම</i>&#x20;(<i>pārima</i>, “farther”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pāsāda (“palace”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pāsādo, nominative singular of <i>පාසාද</i> &#x20;(pāsāda, “palace”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Particle</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pi</li></ol><p><b>Conjunction</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> pi (“even”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> piṭṭhi</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adverb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> piṭṭhito piṭṭhito</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> putta (“son”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> putto, <i>which is</i> nominative singular of <i>පුත‍්ත</i> &#x20;(putta)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> purisa (“man”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> puriso, <i>which is</i> nominative singular of <i>පුරිස</i> &#x20;(purisa, “man”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> phandati (“to stir”)</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li>masculine/neuter locative singular of <i>ඵන්‍දන‍්ත්</i> &#x20;(phandant), present participle of the verb above</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> phandayati, causative of <i>ඵන්‍දති</i> &#x20;(phandati, “to do”) <i>and an</i> alternative form of <i>ඵන්‍දෙති</i>&#x20;(<i>phandeti</i>)</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> phandayati, <i>which is</i> masculine/neuter locative singular of <i>ඵන්‍දයන‍්ත්</i> &#x20;(phandayant), <i>present participle of the verb above</i></li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> phandayant, present partitive of <i>ඵන්‍දෙති</i> &#x20;(phandeti), <i>which see</i>, causative of <i>ඵන්‍දති</i> &#x20;(phandati, “to stir”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> phandāpayati, causative of <i>ඵන්‍දති</i> &#x20;(phandati, “to stir”) <i>and an</i> alternative form of <i>ඵන්‍දාපෙති</i>&#x20;(<i>phandāpeti</i>)</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> phandāpayati, which is masculine/neuter locative singular of <i>ඵන්‍දාපයන‍්ත්</i> &#x20;(phandāpayant), present participle of the verb above</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> phandāpayant, present participle of <i>ඵන්‍දාපෙති</i> &#x20;(phandāpeti), causative of <i>ඵන්‍දති</i> &#x20;(phandati, “to stir”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> phandāpeti, <i>which see</i>, (double) causative of <i>ඵන්‍දති</i> &#x20;(phandati, “to stir”)</li></ol><p><