oun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> viveka (“detachment”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> viveko, nominative singular of <i>විවෙක</i> (“detachment”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> viharati (“to dwell”)</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> viharati, <i>which is</i> masculine and neuter locative singular of <i>විහරන‍්ත්</i> &#x20;(viharant), <i>present participle of the verb above</i></li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> viharant, <i>which is</i> present active participle of <i>විහරති</i> &#x20;(viharati, “to dwell”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> vutta, <i>which is</i> past participle of <i>වදති</i> &#x20;(vadati)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> vedeha (“Videhan”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> vedeho, nominative singular masculine of <i>වෙදෙහ</i> &#x20;(vedeha, “Videhan”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> vera (“hatred”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> veraṃ, nominative/accusative singular of <i>වෙර</i> &#x20;(vera, “hatred”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Pronoun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> vo, which is accusative/instrumental/genitive/dative plural of <i>ත්‍වං</i> &#x20;(tvaṃ, “you”)</li></ol><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> vo, which is nominative singular of <i>ව</i> &#x20;(va, “letter 'v'”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Pronoun</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> sa, which is nominative singular of <i>ත</i> &#x20;(ta, “he, it”)</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Sinhala script form of</i> sa, which is nominative singula