b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> bālo, <i>which is</i> nominative singular masculine of <i>ဗာလ</i> &#x20;(bāla, “young, ignorant”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> bindu</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> bīja</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> bījā, ablative singular of <i>ဗီဇ</i> &#x20;(bīja, “seed”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Proper Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> buddha (“Buddha”)</li></ol><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> buddha (“buddha”)</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> buddha, past participle of <i>ဗုဇ္ဈတိ</i> &#x20;(bujjhati, “to understand”)</li><li>(<i>Mon</i>) <i>Burmese script form of</i> buddha, past participle of <i>ဗုဇ္ၛတိ</i> &#x20;(bujjhati, “to understand”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> buddhāya, <i>which is</i> inflection of <i>ဗုဒ္ဓ</i>:## dative singular masculine/neuter## instrumental/genitive/ablative/dative/locative singular feminine &#x20;(buddha, “enlightened”)</li></ol><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> buddhāya, <i>which is</i> dative singular of <i>ဗုဒ္ဓ</i> &#x20;(buddha, “buddha”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Proper Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> buddho, <i>which is</i> nominative singular of <i>ဗုဒ္ဓ</i> &#x20;(buddha, “Buddha”)</li></ol><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> buddho, <i>which is</i> nominative singular of <i>ဗုဒ္ဓ</i> &#x20;(buddha, “buddha”)</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> buddho, <i>which is</i> nominative singular masculine of <i>ဗုဒ္ဓ</i> &#x20;(buddha), <i>which is</i> past participle of <i>ဗုဇ္ဈတိ</i> &#x20;(bujjhati, “to understand”)</li><li>(<i>Mon</i>) <i>Burmese script form of</i> buddho, <i>which is</i> nominative singular masculine of <i>ဗုဒ္ဓ</i> &#x20;(buddha), <i>which is</i> past participle of <i>ဗုဇ္ၛတိ</i> &#x20;(bujjhati, “to understand”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> buddhaṃ, <i>which is</i> inflection of <i>ဗုဒ္ဓ</i>:## accusative singular masculine/feminine/neuter## nominative singular neuter &#x20;(buddha, “enlightened”)</li></ol><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> buddhaṃ, <i>which is</i> accusative singular of <i>ဗုဒ္ဓ</i> &#x20;(buddha, “the Buddha”)</li></ol><p><b>Proper Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> buddhaṃ, <i>which is</i> accusative singular of <i>ဗုဒ္ဓ</i> &#x20;(buddha, “the Buddha”)</li><li><i>Burmese script, Mon variant form of</i> buddhaṃ, <i>which is</i> accusative singular of <i>ဗုဒ္ဓ</i> &#x20;(buddha, “the Buddha”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> byaggha</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Proper Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> brahmā, <i>which is</i> nominative singular of <i>ဗြဟ္မန်</i> &#x20;(brahman, “Brahma”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> brāhmaṇa (“brahmin”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> bhagavato, <i>which is</i> genitive/dative singular of <i>ဘဂဝန္တ်</i> &#x20;(bhagavant, “"Fortunate One"”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> bhagavant</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Devanagari script form of</i> bhagavā, <i>which is</i> nominative/vocative singular of <i>ဘဂဝန္တ်</i> &#x20;(bhagavant, “fortunate one”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> bhaya (“fear”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> bhayaṃ, nominative/accusative singular of <i>ဘယ</i> &#x20;(bhaya, “fear”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li>state of existence</li></ol><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> bhava, <i>which is an</i> inflection of <i>ဘဝတိ</i>:## imperfect active first/third-person singular## imperative active second-person singular &#x20;(bhavati, “to become”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> bhāsā (“language”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> bhikkhā (“alms”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> bhikkhu (“beggar”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> bhikkhunī (“Buddhist nun”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> bhu, <i>which is</i> vocative singular of <i>ဘူ</i> &#x20;(bhū, “the earth”)</li><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> bhu, <i>which is</i> vocative singular of <i>ဘူ</i> &#x20;(bhū, “eyebrow”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> bhū (“the earth”)</li><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> bhū (“eyebrow”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> bhūmi</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Particle</b></p><ol><li>(<i>vocative</i>) <i>Burmese script form of</i> bho (“friend”)</li><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> bho, <i>which is</i> vocative singular/plural of <i>ဘဝန္တ်</i> &#x20;(bhavant, “sir”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> bhoga</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> makuṭa</li></ol><p>Borrowed from Dravidian, compare Modern Tamil <i>முகடு</i> (mukaṭu), Sanskrit <i>मुकुट</i> (mukuṭa, “crown”) (a borrowing).</p></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> maṅgala (“auspicious”)</li></ol><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> maṅgala (“blessing”)</li></ol></ht