html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> mahiṃso, nominative singular of <i>မဟိံသ</i> &#x20;(mahiṃsa, “buffalo”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> mātaṅga (“elephant”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> mātaṅgo, nominative singular of <i>မာတင်္ဂ</i> &#x20;(mātaṅga, “elephant”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> mātar (“mother”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> mātā, which is nominative/vocative singular of <i>မာတရ်</i> &#x20;(mātar, “mother”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> mātāpitar (“mother and father”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> mātāpitu, <i>which is</i> inflection of <i>မာတာပိတရ်</i>:## combining form## alternative stem &#x20;(mātāpitar, “mother and father”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> mātikā (“water course; table of contents”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> māra (“distraction”)</li></ol><p><b>Proper Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> māra (“Mara”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> mālā</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> māsa (“month”)</li><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> māsa (“mungo bean”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> mukhadvāra (“entrance of the mouth”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> mukhadvāraṃ, <i>which is</i> nominative/accusative singular of <i>မုခဒွါရ</i> &#x20;(mukhadvāra, “entrance of the mouth”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> 