</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> yamakaṃ, <i>which is</i> inflection of <i>ယမက</i>:## nominative singular neuter## accusative singular masculine/neuter &#x20;(yamaka, “double, twin”)</li></ol><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> yamakaṃ, <i>which is</i> accusative singular of <i>ယမက</i> &#x20;(yamaka, “twin”)</li><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> yamakaṃ, <i>which is</i> nominative/accusative singular of <i>ယမက</i> &#x20;(yamaka, “pair”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Pronoun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> yā</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> yāyī, <i>which is</i> inflection of <i>ယာယိန်</i>:## nominative singular masculine## nominative/vocative/accusative plural masculine/neuter &#x20;(yāyin, “going”)</li></ol><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> yāyī, <i>which is</i> inflection of <i>ယာယိန်</i>:## nominative singular## nominative/vocative/accusative plural &#x20;(yāyin, “goer”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> yutti</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> yoni (“womb”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Pronoun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> yaṃ, which is accusative singular of <i>ယ</i> &#x20;(ya, “who (m)”)</li><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> yaṃ, which is accusative singular of <i>ယာ</i> &#x20;(yā, “who (f)”)</li><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> yaṃ, which is nominative/accusative singular of <i>ယ</i> &#x20;(ya, “which”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> ra (“the Pali letter 'r'”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> raṭṭha</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> rasa (“taste”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Burmese script form of</i> rā, a