ssu, <i>which is</i> third-person plural optative active of <i>ᩋᨲ᩠ᨳᩥ</i> &#x20;(atthi, “to be”)</li></ol><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Tai Tham script form of</i> assu (“tear”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Tai Tham script form of</i> aṅga</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Tai Tham script form of</i> ācariya</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Tai Tham script form of</i> ārāma</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Tai Tham script form of</i> ārāmo, nominative singular of <i>ᩋᩣᩁᩣᨾ</i> &#x20;(ārāma, “pleasure”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Tai Tham script form of</i> āhuneyya (“worthy of adoration or offerings”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li>misspelling of <i>ᩋᩣᨿᩩᩅᨯ᩠ᨰᨶ</i> (āyuvaḍḍhana), <i>Tai Tham script form of</i> āyuvaḍḍhana (“with extended lifespan”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li>A <i>Tai Tham script form of</i> āyuvaḍḍhano, <i>which is</i> nominative singular masculine of <i>ᩋᩣ᩠ᨿᩩᩅᩢᨰᨶ</i> (“with extended lifespan”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Tai Tham script form of</i> opanayika (“leading to”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Particle</b></p><ol><li><i>Tai Tham script form of</i> itipi (“indeed”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Particle</b></p><ol><li><i>Tai Tham script form of</i> itipi</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Tai Tham script form of</i> ima (“this”)</li></ol><p><b>Pronoun</b></p><ol><li><i>Tai Tham script form of</i> ima (“this”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Tai Tham script form of</i> uttama</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Tai Tham script form of</i> uttamaṅga</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Tai Tham script form of</i> uttamo, <i>which is</i> nominative singular masculine of <i>ᩏᨲ᩠ᨲᨾ</i> &#x20;(uttama, “utmost”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Tai Tham script form of</i> udariya (“stomach contents”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Tai Tham script form of</i> upajjhāya (“teacher”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Numeral</b></p><ol><li><i>Tai Tham script form of</i> eka</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Numeral</b></p><ol><li><i>Tai Tham script form of</i> ekavīsati (“twenty one”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Tai Tham script form of</i> eko, <i>which is</i> nominative singular masculine of <i>ᩑᨠ</i> &#x20;(eka, “one”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Particle</b></p><ol><li><i>Tai Tham script form of</i> evaṃ</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Tai Tham script form of</i> ehipassika</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Tai Tham script form of</i> ehipassika</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Tai Tham script form of</i> opanayika</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Tai Tham script form of</i> obhāsetvā, <i>which is</i> absolutive of <i>ᩒᨽᩣᩈᩮᨲᩥ</i> &#x20;(obhāseti), <i>which is</i> causative of <i>ᩒᨽᩣᩈᨲᩥ</i> &#x20;(obhāsati, “to shine”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Tai Tham script form of</i> obhāseti (“to make shine”)</li></ol><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Tai Tham script form of</i> obhāseti, <i>which is</i> masculine and neuter locative singular of <i>ᩒᨽᩣᩈᩮᨶ᩠ᨲ᩺</i> &#x20;(obhāsent), <i>present participle of the verb above</i></li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li>firm, fixed, rigid</li></ol><p>Inherited from Sanskrit <i>दृळ्ह</i> (dṛḷha), from Proto-Indo-Aryan <i>&#42;dr̥ẓḍʰás</i>, from Proto-Indo-European <i>&#42;dʰerǵʰ-</i> (“to be firm, hard”).</p></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li>to place aside, to save, to leave out</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Preposition</b></p><ol><li>except for</li></ol><p>The preposition arises form the sense of 'to leave out' of the verb.</p></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li>standing up</li><li>in some fixed location</li><li>of some particular behaviour</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li>stability</li><li>duration, continuance</li></ol><p>From Sanskrit <i>स्थिति</i> (sthiti).</p></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li>place</li><li>state, -hood</li><li>reason</li></ol><p>Inherited from Sanskrit <i>स्थान</i> (sthāna, “place, state”).</p></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adverb</b></p><ol><li>when appropriate</li></ol><p>Locative singular of <i>ṭhāna</i> (“place”), which has acquired a special force.</p></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li>commentary, subcommentary, gloss</li></ol><p>From Sanskrit <i>टीका</i> (ṭīkā, “commentary”).</p></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Particle</b></p><ol><li>like, as</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Brahmi script form of</i> akkhi</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Brahmi script form of</i> aggi (“fire”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Brahmi script form of</i> acci</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Brahmi script form of</i> accha</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Brahmi script form of</i> accharā (“celestial nymph”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Brahmi script form of</i> accho, nominative singular of <i>𑀅𑀘𑁆𑀙</i> &#x20;(accha, “bear”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Brahmi script form of</i> ajagara</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adverb</b></p><ol><li><i>Brahmi script form of</i> ajja (“today”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Numeral</b></p><ol><li><i>Brahmi script form of</i> aṭṭha (“eight”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Brahmi script form of</i> aṭṭhama</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Brahmi script form of</i> aṭṭhamo, nominative singular masculine of <i>𑀅𑀝𑁆𑀞𑀫</i> &#x20;(aṭṭhama, “eighth”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Brahmi script form of</i> aṭṭhi (“bone”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Brahmi script form of</i> aḍḍhamāsa (“fortnight”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Verb</b></p><ol><li><i>Brahmi script form of</i> atthi (“to be”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adverb</b></p><ol><li><i>Brahmi script form of</i> adhunā (“now”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Brahmi script form of</i> amacca</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Pronoun</b></p><ol><li><i>Brahmi script form of</i> amhe (“we, us”), <i>which is</i> nominative/accusative plural of <i>𑀅𑀳𑀁</i> &#x20;(ahaṃ)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Brahmi script form of</i> ayya (“noble”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Brahmi script form of</i> aroga (“healthy”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Brahmi script form of</i> asoka (“free from sorrow”)</li></ol><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Brahmi script form of</i> asoka (“Ashoka tree”)</li></ol><p><b>Proper Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Brahmi script form of</i> asoka</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Adjective</b></p><ol><li><i>Brahmi script form of</i> asoko, nominative singular masculine of <i>𑀅𑀲𑁄𑀓</i> &#x20;(asoka, “free from sorrow”)</li></ol><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Brahmi script form of</i> asoko, nominative singular of <i>𑀅𑀲𑁄𑀓</i> &#x20;(asoka, “Ashoka tree”)</li></ol><p><b>Proper Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Brahmi script form of</i> asoko, nominative singular of <i>𑀅𑀲𑁄𑀓</i> &#x20;(asoka, “Ashoka”)</li></ol></html><h3>Pali</h3><p><b>Noun</b></p><ol><li><i>Brahmi script form of</i> asme, <i>which is</i> accusative plural of <i>𑀅𑀲𑁆𑀫𑀦𑁆</i> &#x20;(asman, “stone”)</li></ol><p><b>Pronoun</b></p><ol><li><i>Brahmi script form of</i> asme (“us”), <i>which is an</i> accusative plural of <i>𑀅𑀳𑀁</i> &#x20;(ahaṃ)</li></ol></html><h